    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Standard errors provide rough guides to the accuracy of variance-component estimates, and to estimate them, we require the sampling variances of the observed mean squares. Under the assumptions of normality and balanced design, a useful (and general) result is that the observed mean squares extracted from an analysis of variance are distributed independently with expected sampling variance",
      "source_page": 575,
      "printed_page": 555,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p009:b5"
      ],
