    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The standard errors of the estimated within-family, among-family, and total phenotypic variance estimates are obtained by substituting observed mean squares into Equations 18.20a,c,d and taking square roots. Since the accuracy of the resultant standard errors depends on the accuracy of the observed mean squares, the standard errors are not very reliable if the degrees of freedom are small. Hence, the reference to “large-sample” estimators.",
      "source_page": 576,
      "printed_page": 556,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p010:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        126.0,
