    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The standard error of $ h^{2} $ derived by half-sib analysis is estimated by $ 4\\sqrt{\\mathrm{Var}(t)} $. Again, the accuracy of this expression increases with the number of families in an analysis.",
